Sval: each private window is a browsing session of its own

A private window's first tab opens in a cookie jar of its own
(SvalPrivateJars), and its new tabs follow it through
gBrowser.defaultUserContextId; a window a page opened keeps its opener's,
as Gecko gives it. Any other tab opened in a private window is given the
window's jar, whatever was asked for, and a private popup's links open in
the window whose session it shares, or in a window of their own. Switch to
tab offers a private window only its own session's tabs, and the content
pref service, the last download folder, and the tab group menus keep each
private session apart too. The jar has to be chosen as the first browser is
made, in _setupInitialBrowserAndTab, which every private window reaches, the
first one under permanent private browsing included; nothing earlier sees
them all. Tabs never move into or out of a private window: the swap refuses
it, the moves to a new window do nothing, and the tab menu leaves "Move to
New Window" out. Each private window lists only the tabs closed in it, and
only its own downloads, in the panel, the toolbar button and
about:downloads. A private window's site zoom is held on the window
(SvalPrivateZoom), and no favicon a private page shows is written to the
profile. No chrome API reaches these: each is decided inside the function
patched, before any event fires.

